  "body": "Stacked on #2342 (merge #2342 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nThe Tormach cumulative A-travel refusal now names a remedy.\nIt asks for a machine with verified A travel wide enough for the whole operation.\nIt explains that Rotary Offset cutting levels cover two laps plus seam padding.\n\n## Cause\n\nPathPilot counts A cumulatively.\nRotary Offset cutting levels exceed the microARC file's stated -360..360 travel.\nThe old refusal explained the limit but gave no remedy.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/post/tests/tormach_rotary_travel.rs`:\n\n- `positive_a_overtravel_names_the_rotary_offset_limit_and_remedy`\n- `negative_a_overtravel_names_the_rotary_offset_limit_and_remedy`\n- `rotary_offset_at_either_a_travel_boundary_still_posts`\n\nBoth overtravel pins failed before the fix.\nThe boundary control passed before the fix.\nAll three pass after the fix.\nThe refusal pins also check that the refused target is never written.\n\nRestoring the upstream/main post failed all three tests.\nRestoring the fixed post passed all three tests.\nRestoring the parent #2342 post failed both diagnostic pins and passed the boundary control.\nRestoring the fix passed all three tests again.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 589 steps, 0 failed, 34.8 minutes.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\nThe inherited compile-cache wrapper stalled once.\nDisabling the wrapper let the required checks complete.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone for #2344.\nThe stack inherits #2342's `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc`.\nThe raw comparison against upstream/main also shows differences from the older parent base.\nThose inherited differences were inspected.\nThis patch changes no NC or CL file relative to #2342.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe reported round-bar rough was not generated.\nNo program ran in the PathPilot Hub or on hardware.\nThe rough remains refused on the microARC file's stated -360..360 travel.\nThis patch changes no toolpath, feed or machine limit.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2342 changes `indexFor` in `assets/posts/tormach.cps`.\nThis branch starts at its head `f29c92bd1`.\nPR #2346 inherits the same function from #2342.\nIt makes no independent edit to this refusal.\n\nChangelog: Tormach cumulative A-travel refusals explain Rotary Offset seam coverage and name a verified wider-travel machine remedy.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nFixes #2344\n",
